{
  "note": [
    "Engine cases for the EMITTER'S OWN hydration output. The hand-written",
    "probe at jl4/tests-cli/fixtures/dmn-hydration-probe/ pins that the boxed-",
    "context idiom evaluates; this file pins that jl4-core/src/L4/Dmn/Lower.hs",
    "emits that idiom correctly, which is the stronger claim and the one that",
    "goes red if the LOWERING breaks rather than the engine.",
    "",
    "Read the hydrated records for the topological sort: `total_income` is the",
    "SUM of the two stored entries and `band` is computed FROM `total_income`,",
    "yet `band` is declared FIRST in hydration.l4. If the exporter emitted",
    "entries in declaration order, `band` would read an unbound name, FEEL",
    "would answer null, and `band` and `band_width` would both be null here",
    "rather than wrong-but-present. That is the whole reason these cases assert",
    "the hydrated records in full instead of only the decisions downstream.",
    "",
    "`capped_bonus` is null in case B: that is the CORRECT L4 answer (NOTHING),",
    "licensed by the explicit null in `expect`. Cases that avoided the absent",
    "branch would be green and would measure nothing.",
    "",
    "Case D supplies a NULL source record, and both engines agree exactly on what",
    "that produces. It is a MEASURED BOUNDARY rather than a happy path: the stored",
    "entries answer null, `total_income` (null + null) answers null, and then",
    "`band` -- whose body is `if total_income >= 100000 then 3 else if ... then 2",
    "else 1` -- takes the ELSE branch twice, because a non-boolean FEEL condition",
    "yields null and null is not true. So `band` is 1 and `band_width` is 25000: a",
    "PLAUSIBLE, NON-NULL derived component computed from an absent record. L4 has",
    "no null record, so no L4 program can ask this question; the DMN model can be",
    "asked it, and answers without complaint. Recorded here so the boundary is",
    "visible rather than assumed away -- see DMN-EXPORT-PROGRAM-MODEL-SPEC.md",
    "§4.4.6. Measured 2026-07-31: KIE 8.44.0.Final and zeebe-dmn 8.7.6 return",
    "byte-identical values."
  ],
